---
import Doc from '@layouts/Doc.astro';
import Container from '@components/Container.astro';
import Section from '@components/Section.astro';
import CodeBlock from '@components/CodeBlock.astro';
import Card from '@components/Card.astro';
import DataTable from '@components/DataTable.astro';
---

<Doc title="OpenChamber Installation" description="Install the vstack OpenChamber extension for workflow visualization">
  <Section id="installation" gap="l" aria-labelledby="install-title">
    <Container>
      <h1 id="install-title">OpenChamber Installation</h1>
      <p class="lead">Install the vstack workflow visualization extension for OpenChamber.</p>

      <h2>Prerequisites</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>OpenChamber</strong> ≥ 1.24.0</li>
        <li><strong>vstack OpenCode plugin</strong> (≥ 0.1.0) generating projections</li>
        <li><strong>Project with .vstack/</strong> directory containing projections</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="margin-top: var(--space-2xl);">Installation Methods</h2>

      <div class="pillar-grid">
        <Card title="Extension Manager (Recommended)" description="Install via OpenChamber's built-in extension manager" actionLabel="Open Settings" actionHref="#" badgeLabels={["Easiest"]} badgeVariants={["info"]} />
        <Card title="Git URL" description="Install directly from GitHub repository" actionLabel="View Repo" actionHref="https://github.com/vipintom/vstack-openchamber" badgeLabels={["Latest"]} badgeVariants={["pass"]} />
        <Card title="Manual Build" description="Clone, build, and load unpacked" actionLabel="Build Guide" actionHref="#manual-build" badgeLabels={["Development"]} badgeVariants={["warn"]} />
      </div>

      <h3>Method 1: Extension Manager</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>Open OpenChamber Settings → Extensions</li>
        <li>Click "Install from URL" or "Install from Git"</li>
        <li>Enter: <code>https://github.com/vipintom/vstack-openchamber.git</code></li>
        <li>Enable the extension</li>
        <li>Restart OpenChamber if prompted</li>
      </ol>

      <h3 id="manual-build" style="margin-top: var(--space-2xl);">Method 2: Manual Build</h3>
      <CodeBlock code="# Clone the repository\ngit clone https://github.com/vipintom/vstack-openchamber.git\ncd vstack-openchamber\n\n# Install dependencies\npnpm install\n\n# Build the extension\npnpm build\n\n# In OpenChamber Settings → Extensions → Load Unpacked\n# Select the panel/ directory" language="bash" showCopy={true} />

      <h2 style="margin-top: var(--space-2xl);">Required Permissions</h2>
      <p>The extension requires the <strong>Files</strong> capability to read projections:</p>

      <ol>
        <li>Open OpenChamber Settings → Capabilities</li>
        <li>Find "Files" in the list</li>
        <li>Click "Grant" or "Allow"</li>
        <li>Confirm the permission dialog</li>
      </ol>

      <p><strong>Without this permission</strong>, the panel will show "Files permission denied" error.</p>

      <h2 style="margin-top: var(--space-2xl);">Verification</h2>
      <p>After installation, verify the extension loads:</p>

      <ol>
        <li>Open a project with vstack projections (<code>.vstack/reports/</code> exists)</li>
        <li>Open the sidebar → Panels → "vstack Workflow"</li>
        <li>You should see delivery overview, tasks, quality, etc.</li>
        <li>Also check Pages → "vstack Dashboard" for full-screen view</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 style="margin-top: var(--space-2xl);">Configuration</h2>
      <p>The extension auto-discovers <code>.vstack/</code> in the current project. No configuration needed.</p>

      <DataTable
        columns={[
          { key: 'setting', header: 'Setting', sortable: true },
          { key: 'description', header: 'Description', sortable: false },
          { key: 'default', header: 'Default', sortable: false },
        ]}
        data={[
          ['Poll Interval', 'Auto-refresh interval (ms)', '3000'],
          ['Schema Version', 'Supported projection protocol', 'v1'],
          ['Theme', 'Follows OpenChamber theme', 'Auto'],
        ]}
        emptyState={false}
      />

      <h2 style="margin-top: var(--space-2xl);">Supported OpenChamber Versions</h2>

      <DataTable
        columns={[
          { key: 'version', header: 'OpenChamber', sortable: true },
          { key: 'status', header: 'Support', sortable: false },
          { key: 'notes', header: 'Notes', sortable: false },
        ]}
        data={[
          ['≥ 1.24.0', 'Full Support', 'All features work'],
          ['1.20.0 - 1.23.x', 'Partial', 'Panel works, page may have issues'],
          ['< 1.20.0', 'Not Supported', 'Extension API incompatible'],
        ]}
        emptyState={false}
      />
    </Container>
  </Section>
</Doc>